purpose: TypeScript type definitions and interfaces
common_tasks:
  - Defining data structures
  - Creating API response types
  - Adding component prop types
  - Defining service interfaces
  - Creating utility types
  - Managing type exports
watch_out_for:
  - Keep types organized by domain
  - Avoid using 'any' type
  - Prefer interfaces over types for objects
  - Use discriminated unions for variants
  - Export all public types from index.ts
  - Document complex types with JSDoc
related_files:
  - All TypeScript files import from here
  - /src/services/* (service types)
  - /src/components/* (prop types)
  - /src/hooks/* (hook return types)
test_command: npm run test:types
key_patterns:
  - PascalCase for type names
  - No 'I' prefix for interfaces
  - Group related types together
  - Use generic types where appropriate
  - Const assertions for literal types